<h1>Decline Pec Fly Machine / Lower Chest Machine Fly</h1>
 <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>Exercise Overview
This 3D anatomical visualization demonstrates the Decline Pec Fly Machine (Lower Chest Fly). The video highlights the lower chest muscles in bright glowing colors, illustrating how adjusting the trajectory high-to-low focuses isolation and tension specifically on the lower pectoral fibers as the handles are brought together.

Exercise Name: Decline Pec Fly Machine / Lower Chest Machine Fly
Target Muscles: Lower Chest (Pectoralis Major — Costal Head / Abdominal Head)
Secondary Muscles: Anterior Deltoids (front shoulders), Serratus Anterior

</div></div>
<pre>
<h1>How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1>

<u><b><h4>1. Setup</h4></b></u>
Adjust the seat height higher so that the machine handles sit slightly above shoulder level. Sit upright with your back flat against the backrest and feet firmly planted on the floor.

<u><b><h4>2. Grip & Alignment</h4></b></u>  
Grip the handles with a neutral position (palms facing inward). Keep a slight, soft bend in your elbows and lift your chest high.

<u><b><h4>3. Fly Phase (Concentric)</h4></b></u>        
Exhale as you press and bring the handles together in a subtle downward arc toward the bottom-center of your chest. Focus on squeezing your lower chest muscles tightly at the peak.

<u><b><h4>4. Return Phase (Eccentric)</h4></b></u>
Inhale as you slowly control the handles opening back up, feeling a stretch across your lower pecs without letting your shoulders roll forward.



<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

<b>◉Lower Pec Definition: </b>Specifically isolates the lower chest line (abdominal head) to build lower chest density.
<b>◉Reduced Shoulder Strain: </b>A downward pressing angle places less stress on the anterior deltoids compared to incline movements.
<b>◉Constant Lower Chest Tension:</b> Maintains high resistance directly on the lower pectoral region throughout the full range of motion.


<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps </h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 10 – 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Tone | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 3 – 4 | 8 – 10 | 90 seconds |

Keep your shoulder blades pinched back and down against the backrest to keep the focus purely on your lower chest.
